# Ask first — do not assume

Never invent or guess Digivice / project facts. If something is not explicitly stated in the current message, open docs the user pointed at, or a prior confirmed answer in this chat, **ask**.

## Always ask before deciding

- Which bus or port something uses (USB, I2C, UART, soft-UART, SPI)
- What is already plugged in or drawing power
- Pin numbers, BCM numbers, or remaps
- Whether a device is battery-powered, hub-powered, or Pi-powered
- Preferred approach when more than one option exists
- Scope of a change (docs only vs firmware vs Pi app)
- Pushing, flashing, or running install scripts on the Pi

## Do not

- Pick “recommended” wiring because it is common elsewhere
- Reuse an earlier chat’s stack if the user may have changed it
- Implement a full alternate path and document it as settled without confirmation
- Quietly override user constraints (power, fuse, occupied buses)

## How to ask

- Short, concrete questions (one decision per question when possible)
- List the options you see and wait for a choice
- Only implement after the user answers

## Commit by default

- After completing an implementation, commit the relevant changes unless the
  user explicitly says not to commit.
- Keep unrelated modifications, unknown files, backups, and secrets out of the
  commit.
- Do not push unless the user explicitly requests a push.
